{
  "raw": {
    "https://uthscsa.referrals.selectminds.com/faculty/jobs/vice-dean-for-gme-and-dio-13190": {
      "title": "Vice Dean for GME and DIO",
      "description": "Vice Dean for GME and DIO - UT Health San Antonio Careers Settings Our Culture Our Benefits ☰ Jobs Help Vice Dean for GME and DIO 🔍 San Antonio Hot 📁 Faculty 💼 School of Medicine 📅    26000265 Requisition # Apply for Job Share this Job Sign Up for Job Alerts VICE DEAN, GRADUATE MEDICAL EDUCATION AND DESIGNATED INSTITUTIONAL OFFICIAL The Joe R. and Teresa Lozano Long School of Medicine (LSOM) at UT Health San Antonio seeks a Vice Dean for Graduate Medical Education and Designated Institutional Official to provide energetic leadership and to promote excellence in medical education. This position represents a transformational leadership opportunity at one of the nation’s largest and most dynamic GME Sponsoring Institutions. The Vice Dean is charged with defining and ensuring a healthy clinical learning environment, creating, evaluating, and implementing an ongoing educational improvement model, and aligning GME resources consistent with the institutional mission. Additionally, the successful candidate will be responsible for resident engagement, satisfaction, and quality. Developing and maintaining excellent working relationships with various governing bodies is critical in this role. Advocating for GME and informing key stakeholders of its value are also essential. The Vice Dean will be expected to develop and strengthen relationships with key stakeholders including sustaining the strong relationships with University Health (i.e. Bexar County Medical District) and the South Texas Veterans Health Care and must work collaboratively with the other clinical sites (i.e. multiple other hospitals and ambulatory care sites) in San Antonio. The Long School of Medicine has approximately 984 active residents and oversees 104 GME programs (61 ACGME-accredited) with no institutional citations. The Office of Graduate Medical Education benefits from a committed staff that includes Associate and Assistant Deans, and Program Directors Coordinators and Managers. The Office has also developed a cadre of well-functioning Standing Committees (Education, Compliance/Accreditation, Quality Improvement/Patient Safety, Wellness/Resident Work Life, Programs and a House Staff Council) that play an instrumental role in drafting policies and practices to help ensure graduate medical education programs that meet national standards. The Vice Dean is expected to devote approximately 80 percent of his/her effort to this administrative role, and 20 percent of his/her effort to his/her clinical faculty position, open to more clinical time dependent upon specialty. The successful candidate should have their scholarly activity and professional contributions focused primarily on Education and/or Service. The Vice Dean will be expected to practice medicine. Interested individuals should submit a letter of interest along with a current CV electronically via the UT Health Careers portal at wp.uthscsa.edu/careers/ and look for requisition #26000265 to apply for this position. Inquires may be directed to Shelly Taylor, Long School of Medicine Chief of Staff at taylors4@uthscsa.edu. A full job prospectus will be sent upon request. UT Health San Antonio (UTHSA) is an Equal Employment Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer including protected veterans and persons with disabilities. All faculty appointments are designated as security sensitive positions. Additional Information Benefits Overview UT Health San Antonio offers an excellent benefits package for its employees. Employees who work at least 20 hours a week, with an appointment of at least 4.5 months, are eligible for benefits. Medical - UT SELECT Medical insurance is offered free for fulltime employees and administered by Blue Cross and Blue Shield of Texas. Family members can be added to the plan through payroll deduction. Employees and their dependents can also receive discounted copays and coinsurance when using UT Health Physicians, a network of 800 premier physicians including more than 100 specialists. Employees receive $50,000 of group term life insurance and $50,000 of basic accidental death and dismemberment insurance for free, with options to purchase additional employee and dependent coverage for both at group rates. Dental - Three dental insurance plan options are available for employees and their families through Delta Dental Insurance Company, two PPOs and one dental HMO plan. Both PPO plans allow employees to choose any licensed dentist. Vision - Fully insured Vision Care benefits are offered by Superior Vision Services. Two vision plan options that offer either standard or enhanced vision benefits. Disability - Employees can enroll in the Disability Insurance which provides income if a non-work related illness or injury prevents you from working. FSAs- Employees can enroll in flexible spending accounts (FSAs) to set aside money from earnings before taxes for qualifying dependent day care expenses or out-of-pocket health care expenses. Retirement - Employees are eligible for either the Teacher Retirement System (TRS) or the Optional Retirement Plan (ORP). TRS is a defined benefit retirement plan which UT Health matches employee contributions. ORP is for eligible faculty staff employees. Voluntary retirement programs are also available to invest before- or after-tax dollars with the choice of five quality retirement plan providers. Time Off- A generous leave program offers multiple paid leave options: Front-loaded Paid Time Off: 128 to 208 hours (16 to 26 days) of Paid Time Off based on years of service, given at the start of each fiscal year. PTO may be prorated in year one based on date of hire. Extended Illness Bank: 8 hours (1 day) accrued per month which can be used for illness or injury after one day of Paid Time Off is taken. Paid Family Leave: Up to 240 hours (6 weeks) to care for a spouse, child, or parent after 6 months of consecutive employment. Holidays: 12 set paid holidays each fiscal year. Discounts - Employees enjoy a range of discounts on services, tickets, and gym membership. UT Health San Antonio is an Equal Employment Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer including protected veterans and persons with disabilities. All faculty appointments are designated as security sensitive positions. Previous Job Searches My Profile Create and manage profiles for future opportunities. Go to Profile My Submissions Track your opportunities. My Submissions Similar Listings Pulmonologist - Open Rank School of Medicine  San Antonio 📁 Faculty  Requisition #: 19001489 Open Rank Advanced Endoscopy Gastroenterologist - Gastroenterology (MSRH) School of Medicine  San Antonio 📁 Faculty  Requisition #: 24001126 Musculoskeletal Radiologist School of Medicine  San Antonio 📁 Faculty  Requisition #: 19002188 View More Listings Jobs Help Site Map © 2026 UT Health San Antonio Recruiting. All rights reserved. Find us 7703 Floyd Curl Drive San Antonio, TX 78229 210-567-7000 Contact us Maps and Directions Job openings Stay connected with UT Health San Antonio Policies Accessibility Compact with Texans Compliance Hotline Privacy Public/personal Information UT Health - Notice of Non-Discrimination on the Basis of Sex Veterans Portal The University of Texas Health Science Center at San Antonio participates in E-Verify. Click HERE to learn more about E-Verify.  E-Verify® is a registered trademark of the U.S. Department of Homeland Security. Copyright 2014-2018 UT Health San Antonio | About us Links from websites affiliated with the University of Texas Health Science Center at San Antonio's website (uthscsa.edu) to other websites do not constitute or imply university endorsement of those sites, their content, or products and services associated with those sites. 0 0"
